; recordspawn.eval - a level saved while its monsters are up and about writes
; each one at its SPAWN, not where it stands (code-review C326). Judged by
; tools/EditorTest.py phase 32, on a scratch copy of dungeon-demo.
;
; eval_arena's six skeletons as filed, then a fight: the swarm at 13,13 killed
; where it lies, and the party stood between the coward (12,1) and the skeleton
; (12,6) until they have noticed it and left their squares. The editor is a
; live view, so this is what any inspector Save or `savemap` met: the .ent
; writer took each monster's CURRENT square while its facing and leash came
; from the spawn, and every patrol, chase and corpse moved its authored spawn
; in the git tree. EditorTest checks the fight happened (a monster off its
; square, one dead, one aware), then compares eval_arena.ent's monster lines
; with the copy's as made, byte for byte.

logecho on
reset
timescale 0
lockstep on
seed 11
echo --- before ---
monsters
; The swarm, killed where it lies (the party faces it from the square north).
tp 13 12
face s
effect bleed ahead 999 2
step 1
; Among the others, healed between bouts so nobody falls.
tp 12 3
face s
step 3
heal
step 3
heal
step 3
heal
step 3
heal
step 3
heal
step 3
heal
step 3
heal
echo --- after ---
monsters
savemap
echo --- end ---
